{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/10118-requesting-help-with-a-ghost-concept","id":10118,"title":"Requesting help with a Ghost concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T18:34:44-08:00","id":10118,"title":"Requesting help with a Ghost concept","content":"So, I'm trying to whip up a pretty strong ghost and I'm basing it off of the novel &quot;Virgin Suicides.&quot; The ghost will be an amalgamation of the Lisbon sisters and the only real idea I have floating around in my head is that a house they &quot;occupy&quot; becomes incredibly oppressive and the actions and feelings of any residents slowly mutate into reclusive and depressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:28:26-08:00","id":15263,"title":"","content":"Just what are you asking about, numina suggestions? Influence suggestions if you're using gmc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:18:12-08:00","id":15625,"title":"","content":"*A small, egg-shaped rock falls out of the White-Wolf-Forums, and EXPLODES into this thread: Shake emerges, dusting off his hat and cane*<br /> <br /> For the raw deal, you should just do like you're initial instincts tell you. I always do; which is why I'm the #1 P.B.&amp; J. Sammich maker in -ALL- of the Midwest. THAT being said, it's important to stay close to your core concept, while laying ground work for mystery, ambushes, and stabby-bits that will get the players absolutely MAD with excitement. So you said the ghost might be oppressive, or oppressing. Perhaps creating some depression, yeah? Since you're having this happen in a house, you have a wealth of things you can muse with. Say for example, if the house was abandoned, you'd have all kinds of junk for the players to sift through. Maybe leave a Black Diary under some rubble, and just make some weird iddle shtuff happen until they discover it one day.<br /> <br /> Another idea might be that the house was cleaned up pretty nice, sold, and might even have NEW things (-gasp-, I know! New=icky) in it. The players move in and get settled, and like a really bad B.-Movie, all of a sudden, a player finds this one old thing lying around that they hadn't noticed before; or that player sees something odd in the mirror, and when they approach it, nothings there. Just the classics, mano: keep it simple, and be kind of smirky and cheeky through the whole thing, and your players will be building a brick house with everything formulating from their collective brown pants.<br /> <br /> Maybe your ghost can't really affect the real world so much, and they've figured out a way into dreams; so they visit the players there, and perhaps a grand chunk of your story takes place in the players dreams; to the point where they all start sleeping at the exact same time, and have the same collective, (there's that word again: I must enjoy it; *cuddles-'collective'*) dreamspaces n'whatnot. The ghost herein might act in a very subtle manner, (may not even fully manifest to the point that they can &quot;target&quot; a single being for a long time.) but is very manipulative. Maybe the ghost starts following the players in their character's lives, and finds small-and-then-huge ways to make the players lives horrible. Maybe it starts off with creating an accident to kill one of the character's favorite cat, but then leads to the character him/herself accidently killing their own GRAMA! (Happened to me once: hated grama-killing-ghosts ever since.)<br /> <br /> While yes, it's important to eventually put some mechanics, dice, and stats to this thing, you really wanna work out the Fabric of what it's concept is first. Does it cry? Does it scream? Does it hate mirrors, or whatnot? What exactly sets it off, or turns it on. Once you get the story/flavor of the ghost down-pat, then you can fit book-made powers, influences, and whatnot into it. Or heck, create your own. Several of the WW books are effing O-mazing at Did-it-myself powers, (generally listed somewhere around the back of each book, eventually.) so just check out those, the criteria for the things you want/need, and then use the Giant Protein Sack behind your Eyebrellas to put it into play.<br /> <br /> *Shake bings the chess-board-ringer-box; it dings*<br /> <br /> Your move, player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1219-shake","name":"Shake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}